---
// AI-Assisted: Claude Code (model: Claude Sonnet 5) - One keyword tag, glossary-aware
// (005-rules-web-enrichment-display tasks T015/T016; spec.md FR-010 through FR-014, US2
// acceptance scenarios 1-5; contracts/render-contract.md sections 2-3).
//
// Used by both the unit page's keyword list and WeaponTable's ability-keyword list, so the two
// places a keyword can appear cannot resolve it differently. Every prop below preserves each call
// site's EXISTING <li> markup exactly (class, and the bare `data-keyword` marker the unit keyword
// list already carried) - this component changes only what goes INSIDE the <li>.
//
// When `resolveGlossary` finds no entry, the content is the keyword text alone: no <details>, no
// `data-keyword-glossary` attribute, no tabindex - the render contract's "exactly as today" case
// (FR-012). When it does, the content becomes a native <details>/<summary> disclosure. Native HTML
// is the whole reason this design works with no script at all: click/tap toggles it, Enter/Space
// toggles it while <summary> is focused, and <summary> is focusable without adding a tabindex -
// three of the four required triggers (research.md section 2), and why SC-007 (zero pointer-only
// interactions) holds even if the enhancement script below never loads.
//
// AI-Assisted note (model: Claude Sonnet 5, cursor-hover-keyword-tooltip branch): hover no longer
// opens this <details> in place. It now shows a cursor-anchored floating preview instead, so a
// reader skimming past several keywords is not left with a trail of expanded boxes shifting the
// page underneath them. Click, tap, keyboard, and the no-JS fallback are all UNCHANGED - they still
// exercise the native disclosure below exactly as before; only the hover trigger's presentation
// moved out of the document flow.
//
// AI-Assisted note (model: Claude Sonnet 5, wargear-abilities web feature Task 2): the hover
// script itself moved out of this file into FloatTip.astro, so LoadoutLines.astro's new
// wargear-ability disclosure can mount the identical enhancement instead of duplicating it. This
// component keeps the bare `data-keyword-glossary` attribute and `keyword-glossary__summary`
// class it always carried (nothing here re-selects on those), and additionally carries
// `data-float-tip` and `float-tip__summary` - the generalised selector/lookup FloatTip.astro's
// moved script now uses for either disclosure kind.
import { resolveGlossary } from '../data/glossary.ts';
import FloatTip from './FloatTip.astro';

interface Props {
  text: string;
  wrapperClass?: string;
  /** Reproduces the unit keyword list's pre-existing bare `data-keyword` marker; weapon ability
   *  keywords never carried one, so this defaults to false. */
  markKeyword?: boolean;
}

const { text, wrapperClass, markKeyword = false } = Astro.props;
const entry = resolveGlossary(text);
---

<li class={wrapperClass} data-keyword={markKeyword ? true : undefined}>
  {
    entry ? (
      <details data-keyword-glossary={entry.keywordKey} data-float-tip>
        <summary>{text}</summary>
        <p class="keyword-glossary__summary float-tip__summary">{entry.summary}</p>
      </details>
    ) : (
      text
    )
  }
</li>

<FloatTip />
